    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "**Detail, manual mask (FLUX 3 Klein)** - ADetailer-style \"inpaint only masked\"\n\n1. Load the image in **Image to fix**, right-click it > **Open in MaskEditor**, paint over what you want redone (a face, a hand, a sword hilt) and **Save**.\n2. Separate painted blobs become separate regions. A painted outline is filled in.\n3. Describe the region in **Prompt** if the default doesn't fit (\"a steel sword hilt wrapped in leather\").\n\n**All settings are in the two groups on the left** (Main settings, Fine-tuning); the titles say what each does. The nodes they feed show the same values greyed out, nothing to change there.\n- **Strength**: 0.3 keeps nearly everything, **0.4 default**, 0.5-0.6 redraws more (fixes broken hands/faces, may drift from the reference).\n- **Work size**: each region (with its context) is enlarged so its short side is 1024 px, long side capped at 1536. Klein's sweet spot is about 1 MP; lower it to go faster.\n- **Seam blur / Repaint edge falloff**: raise them if you see a visible border around a region.\n- Separate regions are done one after another; each uses seed + 1.\n\n**References**: *Reference 1* is fed to Klein for every region, so a face stays the face in the reference. The prompt refers to it as `<ref_image_0>` (and `<ref_image_1>` for Reference 2). No reference? Bypass Reference 1 (Ctrl+B) and drop the sentence with `<ref_image_0>` from the prompt.\n\n*Regions before/after* show each crop; *Before / after* the whole image. Output: `output/detail/`. Transparency is not kept.\n"
   ],
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Tailored for this setup"
  }
